Saphira OpenStack compute role (hypervisor)
============================================

Install this package on every machine that will run guest instances,
then run, as root:

    saphira-openstack-setup-compute

It asks which controller to join, the service password, the provider
physical-network name, the OVS bridge, and which NIC carries tenant
traffic — then configures nova-compute and the neutron OVS/DHCP
agents, fixes every privilege boundary they need, starts the full
libvirt daemon set, builds the provider bridge, and tells you how to
prove the controller sees the new hypervisor.

Safety notes (also enforced by the script):
  - virt_type is probed: kvm when /dev/kvm exists, qemu otherwise.
    Never force kvm on a host without it; libvirt refuses the guest.
  - Enslaving the NIC you ssh through moves your session onto the
    bridge. The script makes you type YES for that. A dedicated
    tenant NIC is always the calmer choice.
  - Re-running is safe; existing config is kept unless --force.

Verify later with:

    saphira-openstack-setup-compute --check

Full story (how-to, pitfalls, do and don't):
saphira-openstack-documentation.
Saphira Linux — "It's so Simple it Hurts."
